WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.969
Here's how Stag Hunt works, for new investors.

2
00:00:02.936 --> 00:00:04.235
Pause whenever you like...

3
00:00:04.202 --> 00:00:06.947
and follow along on your own screen.

4
00:00:06.923 --> 00:00:09.468
Go to staghunts dot com slash login.

5
00:00:09.434 --> 00:00:12.693
Type your email, and click Email me a sign-in link.

6
00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:13.712
Open the email.

7
00:00:13.679 --> 00:00:15.997
Click the link, or type the six-digit code here.

8
00:00:15.963 --> 00:00:18.183
There is no password.

9
00:00:18.616 --> 00:00:19.761
Type your name.

10
00:00:19.727 --> 00:00:22.324
Then the largest check you'd write into one company.

11
00:00:22.291 --> 00:00:24.804
You'll see deals that take a check that size or smaller.

12
00:00:24.771 --> 00:00:26.019
You can leave it empty.

13
00:00:25.986 --> 00:00:27.896
Click Continue.

14
00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:29.364
This is your investor statement.

15
00:00:29.331 --> 00:00:31.012
Pick the line that's true for you.

16
00:00:30.978 --> 00:00:34.042
If none of them are, pick Not accredited.

17
00:00:35.422 --> 00:00:37.144
Read each promise and tick it.

18
00:00:37.111 --> 00:00:39.412
Then click Join Stag Hunt.

19
00:00:47.543 --> 00:00:48.709
This is Home.

20
00:00:48.676 --> 00:00:52.218
If you're accredited, deals open for you thirty days after your statement.

21
00:00:52.184 --> 00:00:55.639
Until then, you can bring deals and start a hunt.

22
00:00:55.623 --> 00:00:57.849
Thirty days later, Home looks like this.

23
00:00:57.816 --> 00:00:59.629
Deals waiting for your call are at the top.

24
00:00:59.596 --> 00:01:01.743
Click one to open it.

25
00:01:04.703 --> 00:01:07.289
Start at the top: what the company does, the round,

26
00:01:07.256 --> 00:01:08.946
and the smallest check it takes.

27
00:01:08.912 --> 00:01:12.593
Below that, the member who brought it says how they know the founders.

28
00:01:12.571 --> 00:01:14.282
Scroll down for where the company is today,

29
00:01:14.248 --> 00:01:17.138
and where it's going, in the founder's words.

30
00:01:17.117 --> 00:01:17.891
Now your call.

31
00:01:17.858 --> 00:01:18.983
Do you want to meet the team?

32
00:01:18.949 --> 00:01:20.331
Click yes or no.

33
00:01:20.297 --> 00:01:23.700
Say whether you've met the founders, and write one line on why.

34
00:01:25.763 --> 00:01:26.991
Click Submit my call.

35
00:01:26.957 --> 00:01:29.018
Your call locks, and it can't be changed.

36
00:01:28.985 --> 00:01:31.791
Only now do you see everyone else's calls.

37
00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:32.812
Want to meet them?

38
00:01:32.779 --> 00:01:34.572
Ask the member who brought it for an intro,

39
00:01:34.538 --> 00:01:36.239
with the button below your call.

40
00:01:36.206 --> 00:01:38.508
They get your email address.

41
00:01:38.487 --> 00:01:40.743
If you decide to invest, use the Invest button.

42
00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:43.100
You invest straight with the company, on your own clock.

43
00:01:43.067 --> 00:01:45.873
Stag Hunt never holds or moves money.

44
00:01:45.849 --> 00:01:47.035
Click Hunts.

45
00:01:47.002 --> 00:01:50.730
A hunt is a group that shares deals, and you start in the first one.

46
00:01:50.697 --> 00:01:53.633
To start your own, type a name and click Start the hunt.

47
00:01:53.599 --> 00:01:55.943
Then invite people by email.

48
00:01:57.904 --> 00:02:01.077
When you meet a founder worth backing, click Share a deal.

49
00:02:01.043 --> 00:02:03.362
Fill in what the company does, where it is today,

50
00:02:03.328 --> 00:02:05.053
and the round.

51
00:02:05.034 --> 00:02:07.178
Your record keeps every call you make.

52
00:02:07.144 --> 00:02:10.495
When outcomes are known, it can show which ones you got right.

53
00:02:10.483 --> 00:02:11.772
That's the whole tour.

54
00:02:11.738 --> 00:02:13.347
Startup investing is risky.

55
00:02:13.314 --> 00:02:14.428
Most startups fail.

56
00:02:14.395 --> 00:02:16.198
And this isn't investment advice.

57
00:02:16.165 --> 00:02:18.230
See you on the hunt.

